{
  "info": {
    "name": "Applicant and Credential Services",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Run in order against the team stack (docker compose up). The setup folder opens a real session through Player and Session, so the session tokens are the real ones.\n\nEverything goes through the Gateway. A client sends Authorization: Bearer <token>; the Gateway validates it, drops the header and tells the service who is calling through X-Player-Id, X-Session-Id and X-Session-Role. Only the last folder sets those headers itself, to check that the Gateway does not believe them.\n\nTwo base URLs, because what a request may reach depends on the door it arrived at. gatewayBaseUrl is the published port, http://127.0.0.1:8080 from your machine. internalBaseUrl is http://gateway:8001, which is not published: it serves the endpoints the contract marks internal, here opening a session, creating an applicant, reading the full applicant with the impostor flag, and validating documents. Reaching it means running inside the Docker network:\n\n    docker run --rm --network pad-team-20_backend -v \"$PWD/postman:/etc/newman\" \\\n      postman/newman run applicant-and-credential.postman_collection.json \\\n      --env-var gatewayBaseUrl=http://gateway:8000\n\nRun it from your machine instead and the internal requests cannot reach gateway:8001: they fail, and so does every request that needs the session or the applicants they create."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup: players and a session",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register moderator",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('moderatorName', 'mod' + Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('moderatorId', pm.response.json().playerId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/player/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{moderatorName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{moderatorName}}@utm.md\",\n  \"password\": \"correcthorse1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register junior mod",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('juniorName', 'jr' + Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('juniorId', pm.response.json().playerId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('juniorPlayerToken', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/player/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{juniorName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{juniorName}}@utm.md\",\n  \"password\": \"correcthorse1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Open a session (as Player would)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', pm.response.json().sessionId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('moderatorToken', pm.response.json().sessionToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{internalBaseUrl}}/session/sessions",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"teamId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"moderatorId\": \"{{moderatorId}}\",\n  \"members\": [\n    {\n      \"playerId\": \"{{moderatorId}}\",\n      \"level\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"playerId\": \"{{juniorId}}\",\n      \"level\": 1\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
